## Architecture

- Flutter talks only to `API_BASE_URL` (HTTPS in prod) — never to Postgres directly.
- **Current backend:** `backend/app/` FastAPI routes `auth`, `courts`, `profiles`, `uploads`.
- **Target backend:** `api/` Hono routes (ADR-0012). ORM: Drizzle. Validation: Zod.
- Local: `docker compose --env-file backend/.env up -d --build` from repo root.

## Flutter integration

- Use `lib/repositories/*` + `ApiClient` with Bearer token from `TokenStorage`.
- New features: add API route + repository method.
- No `Supabase.instance.client` in new code.

## Auth endpoints (planned)

- `POST /auth/register`, `/login`, `/refresh`, `/logout`
- `POST /auth/verify-email`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`
- Passwords: Argon2id server-side only.
- Email: Resend

## Courts / profiles / uploads

- `GET /courts` — approved courts
- `POST /courts` — authenticated create
- `GET /profiles/me`, `PUT /profiles/me`
- `POST /uploads/presign` — **Backblaze B2** presigned upload (JWT)

